     But now we're back to "playable."  If we can't see pools, now we
have sudden-death traps.  What fun!  On the other hand, if we can see
the pool, we can see the pool (especially if it's in a lit room).

:The answer is simple:  don't play the game in race mode.  At least 99% of
:the games I get crushed in are my fault for being in too much of a hurry.
     Speak for yourself.  I have lost many games, NEVER from playing in
"race mode"  (ironically, I have played in "race mode" many times and
made dumb mistakes, but I've never had to pay for them as of yet, e.g.
I've always managed to kill floating eyes.  Usually I only do this in
pretty much lost games to start with.)
     Perhaps you play on a Mac or Amiga where the game has a constant
rythm.  This doesn't happen on a slow workstation or an IBM.  You've
every reason to suspect that you'll hit a key and see the output three
or four seconds later, or maybe you'll see it immediately.
     Again, Nethack does not run in a good environment for a
skill-oriented game.

